# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Never commit anything in this section.
#
# The voucher codes are the booth's money: anyone who can read codes.json
# or a codes CSV can take free photo strips. Guest photos are personal
# data and belong on the booth PC only.
#
# data/secrets.json holds the master and staff codes. Six digits cannot be
# protected by hashing -- a laptop tries all million in under a second -- so
# the only real protection is that this file never leaves the booth PC.
# The booth generates its own on first start; /admin shows them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
data/codes.json
data/codes.json.*
data/secrets.json
data/staff-usage.json
data/cloud.json
data/reporter-cursor.json
data/events.log
data/codes-*.csv
data/import-codes.txt
data/import-*.txt
data/import-*.csv
data/redemptions.log
# Which state printing is in right now. Runtime, not source: committed, an
# UPDATE-BOOTH would carry one PC's setting to the booth and could leave it
# silently not printing -- or start printing during a look test.
data/preview-mode.json
data/server.log
_attic/

# guest photos and finished strips (hundreds of MB, personal data)
output/
!output/.gitkeep

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local clutter
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
.kiosk-profile/
*.log
*.tmp
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
.env
.env.*
